{"id":"401bc4f750ae4719","group":"17","path":"17/17-df-complete-formula.md","title":"Complete Formula over a Theory","display":"df-complete-formula — Complete Formula over a Theory","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Model Theory (Chang & Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)","book_abbrev":"17","label":"17-df-complete-formula","aliases":["17-df-complete-formula"],"display":"df-complete-formula — Complete Formula over a Theory","depends_on":["[[17-df-sentence]]","[[17-df-assignment]]","[[17-df-satisfaction]]","[[17-df-model]]","[[17-df-type]]"],"label_origin":"local-catalog","source_section":"2.3","source_result":"Complete-formula definition at section start","source_pages_print":[97],"source_pages_djvu":[113],"source_verification":"definition compared in supplied DjVu OCR; consistency plus inclusive disjunction is equivalent to source exactly-one condition; arbitrary-T extension retained explicitly","source_verification_history":["definition compared in supplied OCR; local relative-theory formulation extends the complete-theory context"],"legacy_label":"17-df-2.6.1"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Model Theory (Chang &amp; Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"17"},{"key":"label","html":"17-df-complete-formula"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>17-df-complete-formula</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-complete-formula — Complete Formula over a Theory"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"1280f7fa724c1502\" href=\"?note=1280f7fa724c1502\" title=\"17-df-sentence\">17-df-sentence</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"9b641c11eab6e875\" href=\"?note=9b641c11eab6e875\" title=\"17-df-assignment\">17-df-assignment</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"ec1305482f8eec2e\" href=\"?note=ec1305482f8eec2e\" title=\"17-df-satisfaction\">17-df-satisfaction</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"53255a372e5c1ee8\" href=\"?note=53255a372e5c1ee8\" title=\"17-df-model\">17-df-model</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"07adad8c036296f7\" href=\"?note=07adad8c036296f7\" title=\"17-df-type\">17-df-type</a></span></div>"},{"key":"label_origin","html":"local-catalog"},{"key":"source_section","html":"2.3"},{"key":"source_result","html":"Complete-formula definition at section start"},{"key":"source_pages_print","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>97</span></div>"},{"key":"source_pages_djvu","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>113</span></div>"},{"key":"source_verification","html":"definition compared in supplied DjVu OCR; consistency plus inclusive disjunction is equivalent to source exactly-one condition; arbitrary-T extension retained explicitly"},{"key":"source_verification_history","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>definition compared in supplied OCR; local relative-theory formulation extends the complete-theory context</span></div>"},{"key":"legacy_label","html":"17-df-2.6.1"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span> 为一阶语言；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega\">\\(n\\in\\omega\\)</span> 是显示元数，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi,\\psi\\in\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\">\\(\\varphi,\\psi\\in\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\\)</span>。以下对这些输入定义相对后承及完全公式谓词；不同 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span> 分别构成接口。</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span> (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\">\\(T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\\)</span>, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"1280f7fa724c1502\" href=\"?note=1280f7fa724c1502\" title=\"17-df-sentence\">17-df-sentence</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\">\\(\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\\)</span> (formulas in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x_0,\\ldots,x_{n-1}\">\\(x_0,\\ldots,x_{n-1}\\)</span>, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"07adad8c036296f7\" href=\"?note=07adad8c036296f7\" title=\"17-df-type\">17-df-type</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\">\\(\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\)</span> (models of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span>, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"53255a372e5c1ee8\" href=\"?note=53255a372e5c1ee8\" title=\"17-df-model\">17-df-model</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Assign}\">\\(\\mathrm{Assign}\\)</span> (assignments, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"9b641c11eab6e875\" href=\"?note=9b641c11eab6e875\" title=\"17-df-assignment\">17-df-assignment</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Sat}_L\">\\(\\operatorname{Sat}_L\\)</span> (satisfaction, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"ec1305482f8eec2e\" href=\"?note=ec1305482f8eec2e\" title=\"17-df-satisfaction\">17-df-satisfaction</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\models_T,\\operatorname{Complete}_{T,n}\">\\(\\models_T,\\operatorname{Complete}_{T,n}\\)</span> (relations defined here)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\quad\n\\varphi\\models_T\\psi\n\\;\\leftrightarrow\\;&amp;\n\\forall\\mathfrak{A}\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\forall s\\in\\mathrm{Assign}(|\\mathfrak{A}|)\\;\n\\bigl(\n\\operatorname{Sat}_L(\\mathfrak{A},s,\\varphi)\n\\to\n\\operatorname{Sat}_L(\\mathfrak{A},s,\\psi)\n\\bigr),\\\\\n\\operatorname{Complete}_{T,n}(\\varphi)\n\\;\\leftrightarrow\\;&amp;\n\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\n\\land\n\\exists\\mathfrak{A}\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\exists s\\in\\mathrm{Assign}(|\\mathfrak{A}|)\\;\n\\operatorname{Sat}_L(\\mathfrak{A},s,\\varphi)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\n\\forall\\psi\\in\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\\;\n(\\varphi\\models_T\\psi\\lor\\varphi\\models_T\\neg\\psi).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\quad\n\\varphi\\models_T\\psi\n\\;\\leftrightarrow\\;&amp;\n\\forall\\mathfrak{A}\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\forall s\\in\\mathrm{Assign}(|\\mathfrak{A}|)\\;\n\\bigl(\n\\operatorname{Sat}_L(\\mathfrak{A},s,\\varphi)\n\\to\n\\operatorname{Sat}_L(\\mathfrak{A},s,\\psi)\n\\bigr),\\\\\n\\operatorname{Complete}_{T,n}(\\varphi)\n\\;\\leftrightarrow\\;&amp;\n\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\n\\land\n\\exists\\mathfrak{A}\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\exists s\\in\\mathrm{Assign}(|\\mathfrak{A}|)\\;\n\\operatorname{Sat}_L(\\mathfrak{A},s,\\varphi)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\n\\forall\\psi\\in\\mathrm{Form}_{L,n}\\;\n(\\varphi\\models_T\\psi\\lor\\varphi\\models_T\\neg\\psi).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>The first line is semantic consequence between open formulas relative to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span>.\nThe existence clause prevents an inconsistent formula from deciding every formula\nvacuously. The displayed arity is part of the predicate: adding an unused displayed variable can change completeness, so it is recorded as <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span>. This notion is a complete formula, not an atomic syntactic formula.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"17-df-sentence","status":"resolved","id":"1280f7fa724c1502","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-sentence]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-assignme